@orders = http://localhost:5280

### Menu and instructions
GET {{orders}}/

### Submit; copy the returned id and traceId
POST {{orders}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"dish":"margherita","scenario":"normal"}

### First lookup: Redis miss -> PostgreSQL -> Redis SET. Repeat for Redis hit.
@id = REPLACE_WITH_ORDER_ID
GET {{orders}}/orders/{{id}}

### Notification progress: pending -> dispatched -> delivered
GET {{orders}}/orders/{{id}}/notification

### Dependency readiness (PostgreSQL and RabbitMQ; Redis is optional)
GET {{orders}}/health/ready

### Additional scenarios: slow-supplier, supplier-retry, supplier-down,
### sold-out, payment-declined, payment-timeout, notification-fail
POST {{orders}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"dish":"margherita","scenario":"supplier-retry"}

### HTTP 202 stays fast; kitchen trace contains a three-second PostgreSQL query
POST {{orders}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"dish":"risotto","scenario":"slow-db"}

### HTTP 202, followed by failed processing and dead-lettering
POST {{orders}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"dish":"carbonara","scenario":"fail"}
